12	// End-to-end (file in, file out) regression coverage for the shared-intermediate
13	// batch-delete scenario, exercising the public preview/apply commands exactly
14	// as the README documents:
15	//
16	//	R -> M -> B -> H -> T
17	//	     \-> C -/   (H converges on B and C)
18	//	S (root)       U -> V (isolated component)
19	//
20	// The successful batch deletes M and B, repoints C at R, and repoints H at C
21	// and S. These tests pin that preview is strictly read-only, that apply writes
22	// exactly the final graph the report describes, that the refusal case (H left
23	// dangling at deleted B) rejects the whole batch for BOTH commands without
24	// letting C's legal repoint take effect, and that record/upstream ordering and
25	// repeated upstreams do not change a byte of the success output.
